  "normalizations": [
    "Import record: the frozen record (id, kind, title, source, source_id, year) is mapped by scripts/p3_scenario.py onto the nine fields both suppliers import contract admits; commit and fingerprint are deterministic digests of the frozen record, so both arms send identical input.",
    "enroll-institution: enrollment is reused, not rebuilt. Each institution re-fetches its own live credential under the new purpose, which is what reopening an enrollment means for both arms.",
    "mark-signoff: the participant signs the shared draft off. Both arms' `mark_signoff` operations refuse by design (they reject turning a recorded challenge into a sign-off, priority two f50); the sign-off path is `draft_signoff` on Kyoei and the draft host `signoff` on the reference.",
    "publish-release: the shared draft is published, which releases its output to the other participants, then exported as a public package under CC-BY-4.0 after each contributing institution's administrator consents. The consents have no frozen event of their own, so they run inside g11 and g14.",
    "The draft opener (a.lead) has no sign-off event of its own in the frozen scenario; without it neither arm may publish. Its sign-off runs as a non-primary row inside g11.",
    "The frozen expected graph lists p3.draft and p3.draft.v2 as analysis artifacts. Both drivers hold them as the shared draft's ids, and both arms publish contribution text from that draft.",
    "Fault reason `wrong-purpose`: no operation in either arm ever returns that string. The attempt at g08 is the cross-purpose reuse both arms do refuse, and both return `new-grant-required` outside their literal expected value.",
    "Consent delivery: each institution's administrator (the fixture's consent actor) must be able to use the published output. The reference administrator needs the output's own release first (one release row per publication); Kyoei grants its administrators by institution and carries each foreign consent envelope to A itself. Both patterns stay counted where they happen.",
    "Purpose-bound probes: the scenario asks each probe actor to use the collaboration-3 package for purpose p2-continuation with the literal reason `new-grant-required`. Both arms refuse it at the residency/reader boundary first (`not-authorized`): no purpose-check row exists for a public package on that actor yet. Both arms return the same reason; the literal expected string is itemized for both, not scored as a difference."
  ],
